  "tag": "r4b",
  "structural_change": "Native pin audit of the CLOSED r3b view (coll_tp8_colr3_a-r3b-607a7b9b1, TT R 286.1, phi - R, first-load Liberty; results/rtl/qwen_coll_io_1014/native_audit/ot_coll_tp8_col_tile_r3.json): launch 260.5 (sr/s_lo/s_hi/od/ur/ovf) and capture 288.0 (sr_d 136 pins, e_tx 49, tq_wd 18, rst_n 210.5, die_s 252.4), 252 pins over 220/190 although the RTL has a flop on every pin: the recipe-1 kit let timing-driven GPL pull the pin flops into the macro channels (medians 174-176 ps, tails 250-290). r4b = hedge sibling of coll_tp8_colr3_a r4: (1) kit recipe 2 WITHOUT the inhold/outhold pin stages (r3b closed FF +16.96 with none) with the closed leaf's halo 6.48 (r3 crashed GRT-0183 in repair_design at an INV inside the 5.4-um halo of the PQ macro): every pin flop FIRM at its pin (io_flop_at_pins), pin registers kept through synthesis; (2) RTL: rst_n now reaches ONE reset leaf at its pin (u_pr) and the core + six queues take its synchronised release (new PRESYNC parameter: the identical release edge their own leaves gave, cycle-exact), die_s lands in one pin flop (static strap). Benches unchanged (WT 3 exact unit 9 / production 3 PASS, cycles identical; SKEW/SEAM/OWNER mutants FAIL).",
  "purpose": "Qwen TP8 compute-die collective (qfd_io_collective) data column leaf, pin-registered WT 3 (qwen-coll-io r2 10-14, el1014-qwen-coll-io.log). 14 x 32x128 macros (same plan as the closed WT 2 leaf), 244.08 x 237.6, cap M5, recipe 2 (pin flops at pins, pin_reg_split, HB2 pads) with halo 6.48 + macro-edge M5 guard. Composition benches: 8-rank TP8 golden ((P0+P1)+P2)+P3 with Pp = die0+die1, exact unit 9 cases + production 3 cases (WT 3, DEPTH 64 engine, LQ/TQ 128); mutants OT_TP8_MUT_OWNER / OT_TP8_MUT_GATHER / OT_TP8R_MUT_SEAM / OT_TP8R3_MUT_SKEW (s_lo/s_hi pin flop bypassed: slices see words one edge early) all fail.",
